          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The contract distinguishes between repo-controlled rules (potentially hostile, worth disclosing) and caller-supplied rules (the caller's own instruction, noise if reported back). Excluding untracked files is not disclosed; only tracked files removed by repository rules appear in the report.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "textSnapshot": "Problem:\nRepository-controlled ignore rules (.graphignore, .gitignore, .git/info/exclude) can exclude tracked source files from search results without visibility. An agent following the doctrine \"search first\" could receive a narrowed corpus and not know it, leading to incomplete answers presented as complete.\nSolution:\nThe search command now discloses repository-controlled exclusions by:\nAdding a RepoIgnored field to SearchResponse containing the count, source files, and a sampled list of excluded paths (capped at 10 to avoid floods)\nAdding RepoIgnoredFiles to SearchStats showing the count alongside FilesScanned so \"2 files scanned\" doesn't hide the fact that a committed rule removed a third\nEmitting a W_REPO_IGNORED_SOURCE warning on the standard diagnostics channel carrying the first excluded path (so compact agent payloads still surface it)\nRendering the exclusion details at the head of text output before ranked results\nExcluding caller-controlled exclusions (from --ignore-file / --include-file) from disclosure—only repository-controlled rules are reported\nSilencing the field entirely when no exclusions occur (zero-cost in the common path)\nThe contract distinguishes between repo-controlled rules (potentially hostile, worth disclosing) and caller-supplied rules (the caller's own instruction, noise if reported back). Excluding untracked files is not disclosed; only tracked files removed by repository rules appear in the report.",
    "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T19:24:44.899Z",
    "etag": "W/\"2026-08-19T19:24:44.899045Z\""
